# The Cessna 172P Skyhawk's checklists, written in this project's own words
# from its Pilot's Operating Handbook and FAA Approved Airplane Flight
# Manual, 1981 Model 172P, section 4, Normal Procedures, pages 4-6 to 4-10 -
# the handbook docs/ASSETS.md already records for this aeroplane's published
# figures, read here from the copies that file names.
#
# The handbook's order is kept: before starting engine, starting engine,
# taxiing, before takeoff, normal takeoff, enroute climb, cruise, descent,
# before landing, normal landing, after landing. Its figures are kept as it
# gives them.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# **The handbook's speeds are indicated; the simulation reads calibrated.**
# They differ by a knot or so at these speeds, so a band taken from the
# handbook is opened by a knot at each end rather than being quoted exactly
# and then failing on the difference.
#
# The flight model has no carburettor heat, no primer, no magneto switch and
# no parking brake, so the handbook's items for those are the pilot's to
# confirm. Its undercarriage is fixed and its propeller fixed-pitch, and its
# flaps travel to 30 degrees, which is the handbook's FULL DOWN.

phase before-start
confirm Preflight inspection complete and the passengers briefed
confirm Seats, belts and shoulder harnesses adjusted and locked
confirm Brakes tested and set, and the circuit breakers in
confirm Avionics power switch off, as the handbook's caution asks
confirm Fuel selector on both, and the engine primed as required
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.2 Throttle open an eighth of an inch
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture rich
confirm Propeller area clear, master on, and the ignition to start

phase taxi
check propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm >= 500 Engine running
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.4 Taxi at a walking pace on low power
confirm Brakes checked as she first moves
confirm The controls held for the wind, as the taxiing diagram shows

phase take-off
confirm Cabin doors closed and locked, and the flight controls free and correct
confirm Run-up at 1,700: magneto drop within 125, and 50 between them
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 0.0 10.5 Wing flaps nought to ten degrees
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture rich
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Elevator trim set for take-off
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Throttle full open
check velocities/vc-kts >= 54.0 Lift the nose wheel at 55 knots

phase climb
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Throttle full open
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Wing flaps up
range velocities/vc-kts 69.0 86.0 Climb at 70 to 85 knots
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.9 Mixture rich, leaned above 3,000 feet for maximum RPM
confirm Engine temperatures and pressures in the green

phase cruise
range propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm 2050.0 2750.0 Power between 2,100 and 2,700 RPM, no more than 75 per cent
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Wing flaps up
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm <= 0.95 Mixture leaned
confirm Elevator trim adjusted to hold the height

phase descent
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.05 0.7 Power as the descent wants it
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.85 Mixture adjusted for smooth running, full rich at idle power
confirm Fuel selector on both
confirm Carburettor heat as required, to keep the ice out of it

phase approach
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture rich
range velocities/vc-kts 64.0 76.0 Sixty-five to seventy-five knots with the flaps up
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 0.0 30.5 Flaps as desired: to ten below 110 knots, to thirty below 85
confirm Seats and belts secure, and full carburettor heat before the power comes back

phase landing
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 10.0 30.5 Wing flaps down for the landing
range velocities/vc-kts 59.0 71.0 Sixty to seventy knots with the flaps down
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.25 Power off over the threshold
confirm Touch down on the main wheels, then lower the nose wheel gently
confirm Braking the minimum required

phase after-landing
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Wing flaps up
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.35 Throttle back for the taxi
check velocities/vc-kts <= 30.0 Clear of the runway and slowed to a taxi
confirm Carburettor heat cold
